MineWorld {version} — downloadable demo (pre-alpha)

## What this is

MineWorld is an open-source framework for building persistent, modular living game worlds. This demo runs
one world on your own computer: a local server, and a 2D or a 3D client (or both at once) that walks around
in it. It has no AI model and needs no internet connection; the other people in the world follow simple
rules.

## Download

{downloads}

Each archive unpacks into one folder, `MineWorld-{version}-<target>/`. `PLAY.txt` in that folder says how
to start it.

## First open

The demo is not signed.

- **macOS:** double-click "MineWorld 2D". If macOS says it cannot check the app, open System Settings >
  Privacy & Security, scroll down and press "Open Anyway". Or, in Terminal:
  `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine <the unpacked folder>`
- **Windows:** if "Windows protected your PC" appears, press "More info", then "Run anyway".
- **Linux:** run `./MineWorld-2D`, `./MineWorld-3D` or `./MineWorld-2D+3D`, or double-click its `.desktop`
  file in the unpacked folder (your file manager may ask you to trust it first).

## Verify (optional)

- Checksums: download `SHA256SUMS` beside the archive, then `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS` (macOS),
  `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` (Linux) or `Get-FileHash <file>` (Windows PowerShell).
- Provenance (GitHub artifact attestations): `gh attestation verify <file> -R yuema137/MineWorld`.
- The SBOM (`MineWorld-{version}-sbom.spdx.json`) covers the Rust and Python dependency graphs
  (`Cargo.lock`, `uv.lock`) only; Godot's bundled libraries are listed in the archive's
  `LICENSES/godot/COPYRIGHT.txt`. Check it with
  `gh attestation verify <archive> -R yuema137/MineWorld --predicate-type https://spdx.dev/Document/v2.3`.

